3
00:00:11,020 --> 00:00:15,550
今晚，捷豹机械增压版 XKR 对决它的孪生姐妹。
Tonight, Jaguar supercharged XKR versus its twin sister.

4
00:00:15,920 --> 00:00:18,220
修路为什么总是慢得要命？
Why do roadworks take so long?

5
00:00:18,220 --> 00:00:20,420
加把劲！卖点力气啊，你个大老爷们！
Come on! Put it back into it, you, man.

6
00:00:21,100 --> 00:00:25,420
还有 Jamie Oliver 在我们的廉价车里炮制出美味的一圈。
And Jamie Oliver prepares a delicious lap in our reasonably-priced car.

7
00:00:34,420 --> 00:00:38,070
哈喽，大家好，没错！
Hello, hello and yes!

8
00:00:39,300 --> 00:00:41,900
我们今晚还会带大家看……
We'll also be showing you...

9
00:00:41,900 --> 00:00:47,970
我们还会带大家看一个小矮子遭遇的一场超大车祸。
We'll also be showing you a very small man having a very big car accident.

10
00:00:48,600 --> 00:00:49,320
但是呢，
But,

11
00:00:50,500 --> 00:00:54,350
哪怕是以我们对电视制作浅薄的理解也知道，
even we with our limited knowledge of television realize

12
00:00:54,350 --> 00:00:56,250
这种大料可不能现在就放，
that you don't do that now,

13
00:00:56,250 --> 00:00:58,150
必须得留在节目后面，
you have to do that later on in the show,

14
00:00:58,150 --> 00:00:59,900
不然大家看完这节，
otherwise everyone would just watch it now

15
00:00:59,900 --> 00:01:02,000
立马就转台去看《老大哥》的总决赛了。
and turn over to watch the final of Big Brother.

16
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:04,000
所以我们现在这么做，
So what we're actually doing about that is

17
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:05,970
其实纯粹是在拯救你们自己。
saving you from yourselves, really.

18
00:01:05,970 --> 00:01:07,270
没错，这就算解决了一个难题。
Yeah, we are. That's one problem solved.

19
00:01:07,270 --> 00:01:08,500
但当然了，我们还有一个新问题，
But we do have another one of course,

20
00:01:08,500 --> 00:01:11,000
因为在我们停播的这段日子里，
because all the time that we've been off air,

21
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:12,700
老有人跑来问我和杰里米，
people have been coming up to me and Jeremy,

22
00:01:12,700 --> 00:01:13,920
他们总在问：
and they've been saying

23
00:01:13,920 --> 00:01:16,300
《Top Gear》还能回到以前那样吗？
will Top Gear go back to the way it was?

24
00:01:16,300 --> 00:01:19,950
还会是三个普通大老爷们瞎胡闹、打嘴仗吗？
Is it still just gonna be three normal blokes cocking about and arguing?

25
00:01:19,950 --> 00:01:21,650
说实话，这还真是个大难题，
I mean it's actually a problem really,

26
00:01:21,650 --> 00:01:23,100
因为很显然，我们三个老爷们当中，
because obviously one of us blokes

27
00:01:23,100 --> 00:01:25,000
有一位现在已经升级成“戴安娜王妃”了。
has now become Princess Diana.

28
00:01:29,270 --> 00:01:30,500
确实棘手。
It's tricky.

29
00:01:30,820 --> 00:01:32,000
不，他现在真成那待遇了。
No, he really has.

30
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:36,400
不过呢，“戴安娜王妃”本人之前明确交代过，
However, Princess Diana himself has said quite explicitly

31
00:01:36,400 --> 00:01:38,370
说他只想回到一个
that he just wants to come back onto a show

32
00:01:38,370 --> 00:01:40,420
跟去年夏天一模一样的节目里来。
that is the way it was back in the summer.

33
00:01:40,420 --> 00:01:42,720
一点没错，他说求求你们，千万别搞任何变动。
Exactly. He said please don't make any changes, please.

34
00:01:42,720 --> 00:01:44,620
对，他原话明明白白地说了：
Yeah, he actually said explicitly

35
00:01:44,620 --> 00:01:47,150
“拜托看在老天的份上，千万别搞什么大阵仗。”
"for pete's sake, don't make a big fuss."

36
00:01:47,150 --> 00:01:49,650
那是当然。所以现在我无比荣幸——
Absolutely. So it gives me really great pleasure

37
00:01:49,650 --> 00:01:51,850
因为曾经有一刻，我以为自己再也没机会说出这句话了——
'cause I didn't think I'd ever be saying this at one point.

38
00:01:51,850 --> 00:01:53,570
女士们先生们，让我们热烈欢迎——
Ladies and gentlemen, would you please welcome

39
00:01:53,570 --> 00:01:55,550
理查德·哈蒙德！
Richard Hammond!

40
00:02:05,170 --> 00:02:08,120
呃，好吧，这阵仗可真够让人尴尬的。
Oh, well, this is a pretty awkward.

41
00:02:09,450 --> 00:02:10,670
谢谢，我都说了
Thank you, I said

42
00:02:10,670 --> 00:02:12,020
低调点，别搞大……
no fuss, no fu...

43
00:02:12,020 --> 00:02:14,870
噢，不好意思姑娘们，抱歉抱歉，
Oh, sorry gals, sorry, sorry,

44
00:02:14,870 --> 00:02:19,970
借过姑娘们，借过
sorry gals, sorry

45
00:02:19,970 --> 00:02:21,870
我都说了别大张旗鼓的。
I said no fuss.

46
00:02:21,870 --> 00:02:23,770
老兄！
Mate!

47
00:02:23,770 --> 00:02:25,970
哈蒙德！
Hammond!

48
00:02:25,970 --> 00:02:28,250
- 哎呀老兄！
- 盼你回来真是太棒了！
- Oh man!
- I'll be great to have you back!

49
00:02:28,250 --> 00:02:29,850
詹姆斯·梅！
James May!

50
00:02:33,370 --> 00:02:38,050
噢，太尴尬了，真让人无地自容。
Oh, that's embarrassing, really is embarrassing.

51
00:02:38,050 --> 00:02:41,100
搞那个呃……那个舷梯进场，
That's em, that whole stairs thing,

52
00:02:41,100 --> 00:02:44,570
绝对是我这辈子干过最丢人的事。
That was the most embarrassing thing I've ever had to do.

53
00:02:44,570 --> 00:02:46,120
这话你可别对刚在卢顿机场
Well I wouldn't say that to any of the people

54
00:02:46,120 --> 00:02:48,850
不得不从波音737上跳下来的乘客说。
who just had to jump off a Boeing 737 at Luton

55
00:02:48,850 --> 00:02:52,020
我们本来打算搞个像样点的舷梯，你知道那种大号的吧？
We were gonna get some like / ones, do you know the big ones?

56
00:02:52,020 --> 00:02:54,120
但你知道搭一个得花多少钱吗？
Do you know how much they were to gonna be to build?

57
00:02:54,120 --> 00:02:55,300
三百镑。
300 quid.

58
00:02:55,300 --> 00:02:56,270
噢，那倒也是。
Oh, fair enough.

59
00:02:56,270 --> 00:02:58,270
我的意思是，我们确实在乎你，行了吧？你能回来我们高兴极了。
I mean we like it, OK? We are glad you're back.

60
00:02:58,270 --> 00:03:00,220
但花三百镑搭个登机门？
But 300 quid to build a gate?

61
00:03:00,220 --> 00:03:01,400
不，是飞机舷梯。
So no, the aeroplane stair.

62
00:03:01,400 --> 00:03:02,470
我宁可你们别费这心思，多谢了啊。
I wish you hadn't bothered, thank you.

63
00:03:02,470 --> 00:03:04,600
行了听着，眼下大家最关心的头号大问题，
Anyway, listen. This is the big question, I guess,

64
00:03:04,600 --> 00:03:06,120
也是每个人都想知道的。
everybody wants to know.

65
00:03:06,120 --> 00:03:07,550
准备好了吗？
Here ready?

66
00:03:07,550 --> 00:03:09,500
你现在成弱智了吗？
Are you now a mental?

67
00:03:09,500 --> 00:03:10,570
没有。
No.

68
00:03:11,770 --> 00:03:12,770
我没有。
I'm not.

69
00:03:12,770 --> 00:03:14,050
我已经痊愈了。
I'm fixed.

70
00:03:14,050 --> 00:03:16,570
彻底治好了，完全正常，活蹦乱跳。多谢关心。
I'm completely fixed and normal and healed. Thank you.

71
00:03:16,570 --> 00:03:17,520
你拿那玩意儿干嘛？
What are you doing?

72
00:03:17,520 --> 00:03:20,400
呃，万一你待会儿开始流口水，
给你备张纸巾擦擦。
Well you know it's a,
it's a tissue for if you start dribbling.

73
00:03:22,250 --> 00:03:24,200
这四个月来我成天遇到这种事。
That's all I've had for four months.

74
00:03:24,200 --> 00:03:25,200
什么？成天遇到纸巾？
What? Tissues?

75
00:03:25,200 --> 00:03:27,720
不是，是身边总有人围着盯着我看，
No, people hanging around just watching,

76
00:03:27,720 --> 00:03:30,270
就眼巴巴等我眼珠子朝两边斜视、彻底发疯。
waiting for my eyes to point in different directions and me to go bonkers.

77
00:03:30,270 --> 00:03:31,520
我已经好了！我很正常！
I'm fixed. I'm normal.

78
00:03:31,520 --> 00:03:34,400
那你还是出事前的那个你吗？
Are you the same person that you were before?

79
00:03:34,400 --> 00:03:36,120
是啊，我是说医生之前确实担心过，
Yeah, I mean the doctors were worried

80
00:03:36,120 --> 00:03:38,570
毕竟伤到了大脑，怕有什么性情大变之类的。
because it's brain damage, about, you know, personality change or whatever

81
00:03:38,570 --> 00:03:42,670
不过，说真的，现在的我和撞车前的我唯一的区别，
But, no, the only difference really between me now and me before the crash,

82
00:03:42,670 --> 00:03:45,100
就是我现在爱吃芹菜了，以前根本不吃。
is I like celery now and I didn't.

83
00:03:46,350 --> 00:03:48,450
所以你还是那么爱嚷嚷，还是那么好斗？
So you're still shouty, you're still fighty?

84
00:03:48,450 --> 00:03:49,070
没错。
Yes.

85
00:03:49,070 --> 00:03:50,100
那要是我带你去酒吧，
And if I take you to the pub

86
00:03:50,100 --> 00:03:52,570
过了十五分钟你是不是依然想狠狠揍我一拳？
are you still gonna want to punch me in the face after 15 minutes?

87
00:03:52,570 --> 00:03:53,950
想，不过讲真，
Yes, though that's to be honest,

88
00:03:53,950 --> 00:03:55,820
这主要是你太招人烦，倒不是我的问题。
more your personality than mine.

89
00:03:55,820 --> 00:03:58,620
- 你瞧，我通常呆了十五分钟也想狠狠揍他一顿
- 是啊，这完全合情合理。
- You see, I always want to punch him in the face after 15 minutes
- Yeah, that's perfectly normal.

90
00:03:58,621 --> 00:03:59,620
……有时甚至用不了十五分钟
...sometimes less

91
00:03:59,620 --> 00:04:02,370
行了，听着，我认为最重要的
OK, look, the most important thing I think

92
00:04:02,370 --> 00:04:06,350
绝对是确保这种事绝不再发生——我是说撞车。
really is to make sure this never happens again, the crash.

93
00:04:06,350 --> 00:04:08,950
因为你看，你现在的状态就像《怪物史莱克2》里那只穿靴子的猫，
'cause I mean that you're like the cat from "Shrek II" here.

94
00:04:08,950 --> 00:04:11,570
九条命里当真已经折腾掉八条了。
You have used up 8 of your 9 lives really.

95
00:04:11,570 --> 00:04:13,420
所以我决定，今后
So I've decided that in future,

96
00:04:13,420 --> 00:04:16,900
凡是那些死快死快的车，什么兰博、阿斯顿、法拉利，
all the very fast cars, the Lambos, the Astons, the Ferraris,

97
00:04:16,900 --> 00:04:19,100
都由我来照顾，我去……
I'll look after them, I'll...

98
00:04:19,100 --> 00:04:19,870
你去开？
You'll drive them?

99
00:04:19,870 --> 00:04:20,570
对，由我来开。
Yeah, I'll drive them.

100
00:04:20,570 --> 00:04:22,000
看来你的德行也一点没变。
No personality change for you either.

101
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:23,050
那就一切照旧。
Then it's business as usual.

102
00:04:23,050 --> 00:04:26,450
那是自然，我依然像从前一样，是个善良体贴的大好人。
Absolutely, I'm still the same kind thoughtful soul that I always was.

103
00:04:26,450 --> 00:04:27,570
真是感人肺腑。
That's quite moving.

104
00:04:27,570 --> 00:04:29,050
- 行，太精彩了。
- 谢谢。
- OK, brilliant.
- Thank you.

105
00:04:29,050 --> 00:04:31,270
多谢大家，同时也要谢谢你们
Thank you for that and thank you as well for

106
00:04:31,270 --> 00:04:33,370
搞了那么尴尬的走楼梯出场仪式，真是棒极了。
the embarrassing stairs thing, that's great.

107
00:04:33,370 --> 00:04:35,250
如果不介意的话，我还想做最后一番感谢，
There is one more thank you please if you don't mind,

108
00:04:35,250 --> 00:04:36,470
不同之处在于，
difference here is perhaps,

109
00:04:36,470 --> 00:04:37,970
这次我是认真的。
I mean this one.

110
00:04:37,970 --> 00:04:41,200
我想向所有的护士，
I'd like to say thank you to all of the nurses,

111
00:04:41,200 --> 00:04:43,470
以及利兹和布里斯托尔的医生与全体医护人员致谢，
and the doctors and all the staff in Leeds and in Bristol

112
00:04:43,470 --> 00:04:45,250
正是在那里，他们把我重新拼凑了回去；
where I was when I was being stuck back together,

113
00:04:45,250 --> 00:04:48,320
还要感谢约克郡空中救护队的人员，是他们及时把我送了过去；
and the people, Yorkshire air ambulance, who got me there in time,

114
00:04:48,320 --> 00:04:50,570
尤其是，尤其是此时此刻，
and particularly, and particularly right now,

115
00:04:50,570 --> 00:04:52,170
我要感谢每一位写信寄卡片来的人。
to everybody who wrote in.

116
00:04:52,170 --> 00:04:54,250
也许在座的就有人写过，还有电视机前的各位，
Some of the people here maybe, and you perhaps

117
00:04:54,250 --> 00:04:55,950
写信只是为了给我送上祝福。
that wrote in just to wish me the best.

118
00:04:55,950 --> 00:04:58,400
这真的对我意义非凡，帮了我大忙，真心地谢谢你们。
It really meant a lot and helped and thank you for that.

119
00:05:00,570 --> 00:05:01,750
嘿，讲得好！
Hey, bravo!

120
00:05:01,750 --> 00:05:02,950
那楼梯其实挺好看的
The stairs are nice

121
00:05:02,950 --> 00:05:05,150
你的眉毛又没烧掉，
那又怎么了？
You're eyebrows aren't burnt
and what?

122
00:05:05,150 --> 00:05:06,100
你的眉毛——
You eyebrows

123
00:05:06,100 --> 00:05:07,020
噢，都长齐了，
Oh they are fixed

124
00:05:07,020 --> 00:05:08,270
它们本来就坏不了。
they can't be broken.

125
00:05:10,700 --> 00:05:12,300
我们该言归正传了吧？
Shall we resume normal service?

126
00:05:12,300 --> 00:05:14,450
当然，呃，好主意，
Absolutely, err, good idea,

127
00:05:14,450 --> 00:05:16,450
因为我正憋了一肚子火呢。
because I've got a bit of bean in my bonnet.

128
00:05:16,450 --> 00:05:17,600
- 懂我意思吧？
- 懂。
- See what I mean?
- Yeah.

129
00:05:17,600 --> 00:05:19,470
听着，重点是——道路施工。
Listen, the thing is, roadworks.

130
00:05:19,470 --> 00:05:20,850
过去这一年左右，
For the last year or so,

131
00:05:20,850 --> 00:05:23,300
我几乎跟伦敦彻底失联了，
I have been virtually cut off from London

132
00:05:23,300 --> 00:05:26,000
因为他们把牛津环路挖了个底朝天，懂吗？
because they've been digging up the Oxford ring road, OK?

133
00:05:26,000 --> 00:05:29,070
有一阵子，他们把它缩减成了一条单车道，
At one point, they had it down to a single lane,

134
00:05:29,070 --> 00:05:30,400
你只能老老实实开在后面，
and you had to go down that,

135
00:05:30,400 --> 00:05:35,550
在一辆车顶闪着黄灯的工程车“护送”下，以每小时10英里的龟速往前挪。
being escorted by a van with yellow flashing lights on the roof at 10 mph.

136
00:05:35,550 --> 00:05:38,150
骑匹马都比这强，还更快呢。
It'd be better off and quicker on a horse.

137
00:05:38,570 --> 00:05:41,850
然后他们还说，开这么慢是为了保护现场工人，
Then they said it was something you going this slowly to protect the work force

138
00:05:41,850 --> 00:05:44,020
可那儿连半个工人的影子都没有！
but there wasn't a work force there.

139
00:05:44,020 --> 00:05:45,470
他们从来没干过一点正事，
They were never doing anything

140
00:05:45,470 --> 00:05:49,220
因为全躲在工棚里听健康安全讲座呢！
'cause they were in a hut having a health and safty lecture.

141
00:05:49,220 --> 00:05:51,200
他说得一点都没错。
He is absolutely right.

142
00:05:51,200 --> 00:05:52,420
如今搞道路施工，
These days with roadworks,

143
00:05:52,420 --> 00:05:54,650
你压根感觉不到他们在抓紧干活，
you never get that sense that they are getting on with it,

144
00:05:54,650 --> 00:05:56,370
既不麻利也不高效，
doing it quickly and efficiently

145
00:05:56,370 --> 00:05:58,850
完全不为那些受通行困扰的人着想。
for the benefit of those people who might be inconvenienced.

146
00:05:58,850 --> 00:06:00,900
正是那些给他们发工资的人，一点没错。
Who pay their wages exactly.

147
00:06:00,900 --> 00:06:02,200
我是说，这其实特简单。
I mean it's really simple.

148
00:06:02,200 --> 00:06:03,000
把路一封，
Close the road,

149
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:04,450
铺上一层新沥青，
slap some new tarmac on it,

150
00:06:04,450 --> 00:06:06,700
叫管安全健康的那帮人滚一边去，
tell the health and safety people to get stuffed

151
00:06:06,700 --> 00:06:09,670
然后以最快速度把这该死的路重新开放。
and get the damn thing open as quickly as possible.

152
00:06:09,670 --> 00:06:11,670
我是说，这能有多难？
I mean how hard can it be?

153
00:06:11,670 --> 00:06:14,620
噢，我真是太怀念这种心惊胆战的感觉了，
Oh, how I've missed the pang of dread I feel

154
00:06:14,620 --> 00:06:15,820
每当你说出那几个字——
whenever you mentioned the words

155
00:06:15,820 --> 00:06:17,570
这能有多难？
how hard can it be?

156
00:06:17,570 --> 00:06:19,770
好吧，我们马上就要见分晓了。
Well, we are just about to find out.

157
00:06:21,870 --> 00:06:25,400
这就是极其重要的D5481号公路，
This is the critically important D5481

158
00:06:25,400 --> 00:06:29,150
就位于沃里克郡埃文河畔比德福德村外。
just outside the village of Bidford-on-Avon in Warwickshire.

159
00:06:31,050 --> 00:06:34,670
路面坑洼得活像长满青春痘的月球表面。
The surface looks like a lunar teenager's face.

160
00:06:34,670 --> 00:06:37,920
而市政议会表示，要修好这长达1.5英里的路段……
And the council said repairing the 1.5 miles stretch

161
00:06:37,920 --> 00:06:41,670
就意味着要彻底封闭整整一个工作周。
would mean closing it completely for one working week.

162
00:06:43,270 --> 00:06:46,970
这对比德福德的居民来说简直是天大的麻烦。
A massive inconvenience for the people of Bidford.

163
00:06:48,270 --> 00:06:50,350
但这活儿如今归我们接手了，
But we've taken the job over

164
00:06:50,350 --> 00:06:53,700
只要我们讲究效率、拼命苦干、组织得当，
and by being efficient, and hard working and organized,

165
00:06:53,700 --> 00:06:57,650
我们打算挑战在24小时内把它彻底搞定。
we're gonna try and get the job done in 24 hours.

166
00:06:57,650 --> 00:06:58,370
准备好了吗？
Are we ready?

167
00:06:58,370 --> 00:06:59,000
妥了。
Oh yeah.

168
00:06:59,000 --> 00:06:59,920
开搞！
Let's go!

169
00:07:01,770 --> 00:07:04,220
然而刚开始就出了岔子。
Immediately though, there was a problem.

170
00:07:04,920 --> 00:07:09,020
开工前我想先过一遍安全围挡和施工安全须知。
I just wanna go through the barriers, the safety aspects before we start work.

171
00:07:09,020 --> 00:07:12,050
首先是你们必须佩戴的个人防护装备。
First of which is the protective equipment you're gonna have to use.

172
00:07:12,050 --> 00:07:15,450
所有人都必须穿好劳保鞋、工作裤、外套，并戴好安全帽。
You all must have your boots, your trousers, jackets and your hat on.

173
00:07:15,450 --> 00:07:16,720
我们哪有闲工夫听这个。
We don't have time for this.

174
00:07:16,720 --> 00:07:19,550
倒车跟前行时都要注意……
/ would go in backwards as well forwards

175
00:07:19,550 --> 00:07:23,070
任何人步行穿过重型机械施工区，必须有人陪同监护，
So anyone walking beyond the plant must have a chaperone with them,

176
00:07:23,071 --> 00:07:27,360
请务必留心兔子洞，我可不想有人把脚踝崴了或者摔骨折。
Just beware the rabbit holes please, don't want any broken ankles or sprained ankles

177
00:07:27,370 --> 00:07:29,850
光听废话就得听六天，真正干活就一天。
6 days of this and 1 day of work.

178
00:07:29,850 --> 00:07:32,250
交代你们每件个人防护装备该怎么穿……
telling you which piece of PPE(Personal Protective Equipment) you must wear

179
00:07:32,250 --> 00:07:33,550
赶紧让我们开工吧。
Let's just get out of the way.

180
00:07:33,550 --> 00:07:35,550
全员基础防护装备，还有问题吗？
everybody general PPE, any questions?

181
00:07:35,550 --> 00:07:36,970
现在能开始了吗？
Can we start now?

182
00:07:36,970 --> 00:07:39,000
恐怕不行，除非你们把衣服靴子都穿齐整了。
not until you're suited and booted, I'm afraid

183
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:40,100
得了吧，我们这不是穿好衣服了吗。
well, we're dressed

184
00:07:40,100 --> 00:07:41,550
反正没露下体。
Can't see my genitals.

185
00:07:42,500 --> 00:07:46,520
安全说教没完没了地唠叨，我们必须赶紧抓紧时间了，
The safety lecture droned on for so long that we really had to get cracking,

186
00:07:46,520 --> 00:07:50,050
如果还想按原计划在上午9点整准时开工的话。
if we were to begin as planned on the dot of 9 a.m.

187
00:07:52,070 --> 00:07:53,870
这段路全长1.5英里。
Now it's a 1.5 miles stretch.

188
00:07:53,870 --> 00:07:58,550
我们要把它刨开、重新铺沥青、压实平整、画上新的白线，一条龙全包。
And we're gonna dig it up, repave it, roll it, paint new white lines, the lot.

189
00:07:58,550 --> 00:08:00,950
没错，而且由于整条路要彻底封闭，
Yeah, and because the road is actually gonna be closed,

190
00:08:00,950 --> 00:08:02,570
我们必须设置一条绕行路线。
we have to have a diversion set up.

191
00:08:02,570 --> 00:08:04,820
而詹姆斯此刻正在张罗这事儿。
And that's what James is doing right now.

192
00:08:04,820 --> 00:08:06,200
行，这其实再简单不过了。
Right, this is really very simple.

193
00:08:06,200 --> 00:08:07,950
这里是我们的路，在这儿，
Here is our road, here,

194
00:08:07,950 --> 00:08:10,600
很显然这边封死了，因为那是我们的施工地段。
and obviously that's closed 'cause that's where we're working on.

195
00:08:10,600 --> 00:08:13,120
所以谁要是想顺着这儿去阿登斯格拉夫顿，
So anybody wanted to go down there to Ardens Grafton

196
00:08:13,120 --> 00:08:15,300
就得绕一大圈。
would have to go round the block.

197
00:08:15,300 --> 00:08:19,970
因此我要立个路牌，指引他们沿着那头往斯特拉特福方向走，
So I'm gonna put a sign up that takes them towards Stratford down there,

198
00:08:19,970 --> 00:08:22,900
然后在某个地方我再把他们给兜回来，
and then somewhere I'll take them back around

199
00:08:22,900 --> 00:08:25,670
从那边绕一圈，他们就又回到阿登斯了，
back around there and they'll be back around at Ardens.

200
00:08:25,670 --> 00:08:27,300
正好在这条路的另一头。
at the other end of this road.

201
00:08:27,300 --> 00:08:28,470
慢点，稳住。
Easy.

202
00:08:35,100 --> 00:08:38,400
通常这种活儿，他们会用14个人。
Normally for a job like this, they'd use 14 men.

203
00:08:38,400 --> 00:08:40,500
而我们用了32个。
We were using 32.

204
00:08:40,500 --> 00:08:41,920
为了给大伙鼓劲，
And to pat them up,

205
00:08:41,920 --> 00:08:45,800
我准备了一段激昂的动员演讲。
I prepared a stowing motivational speech.

206
00:08:45,800 --> 00:08:48,550
帕特农神庙、金字塔、
the Parthenon, the pyramids,

207
00:08:48,970 --> 00:08:51,020
中国的万里长城，
the Great Wall of China,

208
00:08:51,020 --> 00:08:52,777
每一个都是闪耀的……
Each a shining...

209
00:08:54,630 --> 00:08:58,050
每一座都是人类雄心闪耀的灯塔！
each a shining beacon of ambition.

210
00:08:58,050 --> 00:09:03,550
而今天，先生们，D5481号公路也将名列其中！
And today gentlemen, the D5481 will join that list.

211
00:09:09,300 --> 00:09:12,600
我们要在一天之内把这条路修好！
We shall build this road in a day!

212
00:09:12,600 --> 00:09:18,770
我们重铺的路面将屹立一千年！
Our resurfacing work will last for 1,000 years!

213
00:09:18,770 --> 00:09:21,850
遗憾的是，杰里米讲得又臭又长。
Sadly, Jeremy's speech went on a bit.

214
00:09:21,850 --> 00:09:23,800
但不管怎么说，
But nevertheless,

215
00:09:24,450 --> 00:09:26,850
就在九点零七分整，
on the dot of 9:07,

216
00:09:29,250 --> 00:09:30,700
我们开工了。
we began.

217
00:09:32,100 --> 00:09:34,600
第一项工作是刨掉旧路面，
The first job was to rip up the old surface

218
00:09:34,600 --> 00:09:36,700
这就需要一台道路刨除机。
and for that, we needed a plainer.

219
00:09:36,700 --> 00:09:40,170
按安全规程，开这玩意儿得配三个人，
To operate it safely, you're supposed to use three men

220
00:09:40,170 --> 00:09:44,450
但我们把另外两人调去干别的，决定一个人单挑。
but we put two on other jobs and decided to go it alone.

221
00:09:45,000 --> 00:09:46,520
你来开这台。
You're gonna drive that.

222
00:09:46,520 --> 00:09:46,970
没问题。
Yes.

223
00:09:46,970 --> 00:09:48,220
滚刀把路面刨开，
Teeth dig up the road,

224
00:09:48,220 --> 00:09:50,750
碎石顺着传送带送进卡车里。
rubble goes up there and into the truck.

225
00:09:50,750 --> 00:09:51,500
一点都没错。
Exactly right.

226
00:09:51,500 --> 00:09:52,550
也就是说……
Which...

227
00:09:52,550 --> 00:09:53,920
行了，你开吧。
Well, you can drive it.

228
00:09:57,450 --> 00:10:01,670
与此同时，詹姆斯的交通改道工作开局并不顺利。
James' diversion meanwhile, hadn't got off to a good start.

229
00:10:03,020 --> 00:10:04,400
喂？
Hey?

230
00:10:08,370 --> 00:10:09,950
噢，见鬼。
Oh, cock.

231
00:10:10,650 --> 00:10:12,020
行，准备就绪。
Yeah, all right.

232
00:10:12,700 --> 00:10:14,770
好，总算把刨刀升起来了。
Well, I finally upped the cutters.

233
00:10:15,120 --> 00:10:16,820
转速拉满。
all the revs

234
00:10:17,550 --> 00:10:20,920
走起，手刹，松开。
Here we go, hand brake, off.

235
00:10:27,600 --> 00:10:29,470
动力挂入。
Engine.

236
00:10:30,620 --> 00:10:33,950
搞定，开动，走着。
OK, let's go, yeah.

237
00:10:36,770 --> 00:10:39,400
杰里米，跟上啊大哥，你磨蹭啥呢。
Jeremy, catch up, man, what are you doing.

238
00:10:39,400 --> 00:10:43,420
你特么往后瞧瞧，看看碎石到底进没进卡车！
Just look behind you and see if it's going in the bloody lorry.

239
00:10:43,420 --> 00:10:45,150
别看那路牌！
Ignore the sign.

240
00:10:46,670 --> 00:10:48,370
别看那块路牌，写错了！
Ignore the sign, it's wrong.

241
00:10:48,370 --> 00:10:50,000
詹姆斯表现得烂透了，
James was being rubbish,

242
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:53,320
不过我俩也绝对称不上什么模范员工。
but then we were hardly employees of the month either.

243
00:10:53,920 --> 00:10:55,170
你个大蠢蛋！
Stupid idiot!

244
00:10:55,170 --> 00:10:56,450
我说，别让我分心好不好！
look, stop putting me off

245
00:10:56,450 --> 00:10:58,070
你全倒卡车外面了！
You've missed the truck.

246
00:10:58,450 --> 00:11:00,720
抱歉，对不起，我错了。
Sorry, sorry, sorry.

247
00:11:00,720 --> 00:11:03,350
然后，情况急转直下。
And then things got worse.

248
00:11:03,350 --> 00:11:05,620
杰里米，出了点小状况。
Jeremy, there is a slight problem.

249
00:11:05,620 --> 00:11:06,520
怎么了？
What?

250
00:11:06,520 --> 00:11:09,500
我起步的时候角度好像偏了点，
I've sort of set off with a bit of angle,

251
00:11:09,500 --> 00:11:12,420
现在开到别人路段上去了。
and I'm on the wrong bit of road.

252
00:11:15,520 --> 00:11:17,250
- 这是比德福德对吧？ - 没错。
- This is Bidford, isn't it? - Yeah.

253
00:11:17,250 --> 00:11:20,170
如果想回刚才那地方，
If you wanted to get back to there,

254
00:11:20,170 --> 00:11:22,500
但又不想走刚才那条路，
but without using that road,

255
00:11:22,500 --> 00:11:23,770
走哪边最好？
which is the best way to go?

256
00:11:23,770 --> 00:11:25,470
呃，一直开到环岛，
Err, up to the island,

257
00:11:25,470 --> 00:11:27,150
- 上面那个？
- 对。
- Up there?
- Yeah.

258
00:11:27,150 --> 00:11:29,150
过了环岛第三个路口拐进去。
third turn in after the island.

259
00:11:29,650 --> 00:11:32,670
情况是这样，它本来是笔直往前走的，
What's happened is it goes in the bit of a straight line,

260
00:11:32,670 --> 00:11:33,200
嗯。
Yeah.

261
00:11:33,200 --> 00:11:35,350
然后你想打方向拐回去，它就熄火了。
and then when you tried to turn it back in, it stalled.

262
00:11:35,350 --> 00:11:36,920
所以我正试着把它倒回……
So I'm trying to get it back to the...

263
00:11:36,920 --> 00:11:38,350
多给点油门！
Give it more power.

264
00:11:39,320 --> 00:11:40,570
这就是典型的克拉克森式解题法：
There is a Clarkson answer to a problem

265
00:11:40,570 --> 00:11:42,100
只管大力踩油门。
Just more power.

266
00:11:42,270 --> 00:11:45,770
到目前为止，忙活了四十分钟，我们一共前进了……
So far, in forty minutes, we've done...

267
00:11:45,770 --> 00:11:46,720
- 二十码？
- 20 yards?

268
00:11:46,720 --> 00:11:47,570
- 二十码。
- 20 yards.

269
00:11:47,570 --> 00:11:48,900
你觉得你这么干顶用？
And you think this is helping?

270
00:11:50,170 --> 00:11:53,600
向右，向左，工业园区……
Right, left, industrial estate...

271
00:11:57,320 --> 00:12:00,320
我对目前的进展相当满意。
I'm quite pleased with the way this is going now.

272
00:12:01,370 --> 00:12:02,970
你特么又撞上我了！
You've just hit me again!

273
00:12:03,700 --> 00:12:07,020
我觉得咱们的团队协作越来越默契了。
I feel as though we are working as a team well.

274
00:12:08,250 --> 00:12:10,000
杰里米，我们得停下了。
Jeremy, we've got to stop.

275
00:12:10,170 --> 00:12:11,070
干嘛停？
What for?

276
00:12:11,070 --> 00:12:13,500
因为车斗已经满了，都漫出来了，
Because the truck is full and overflowing

277
00:12:13,500 --> 00:12:15,420
可能根本就卸不下来了，
and it might not be able to tip it out

278
00:12:15,420 --> 00:12:17,900
这就意味着咱俩得拿铁锹去铲了，你个蠢货！
which means we'll have to do it with shovels, you pillock.

279
00:12:18,620 --> 00:12:21,670
为了赶时间，我索性把卡车停在路边，
To save time, I simply parked the lorry at the side of the road

280
00:12:21,670 --> 00:12:23,300
直接就地倒光了事。
and emptied it there.

281
00:12:24,000 --> 00:12:25,500
倒光了！
Empty!

282
00:12:25,670 --> 00:12:28,500
我的同事们对此似乎很不买账。
This didn't seem to go down well with my colleagues.

283
00:12:28,870 --> 00:12:30,070
那是扇大门。
That's a gate.

284
00:12:32,150 --> 00:12:33,170
谁家的大门？
Whose gate?

285
00:12:33,170 --> 00:12:35,950
我……这重要吗？那就是扇门，不知道谁家的大门！
I... Does it matter? It's a gate, it's somebody's gate.

286
00:12:35,950 --> 00:12:38,550
而你把好几吨刨下来的烂路面全倒人家门里了。
and you put several tons of road in it.

287
00:12:38,550 --> 00:12:41,300
而且我也没法……我现在连三点掉头都掉不了了，对吧？
And I won't... I can't do a 3 point turn now either, can I?

288
00:12:42,320 --> 00:12:44,950
没错，你掉不了。那是唯一能掉头的地方。
No, you can't. That's the only turning place.

289
00:12:46,350 --> 00:12:47,820
老兄，你自己看着办吧，自求多福。
You're on your own, man. I'm sorry.

290
00:12:47,820 --> 00:12:48,650
你能弄台挖掘机来吗？
Can you get a digger?

291
00:12:48,650 --> 00:12:49,370
弄不来！
No!

292
00:12:49,370 --> 00:12:53,000
所以是左拐、右拐、左拐，
So it goes left, right, left,

293
00:12:53,000 --> 00:12:55,670
工业园区，右拐。
industrial estate, right.

294
00:12:55,670 --> 00:12:57,420
对，过了工业园区
Yeah, pass the industrial estate

295
00:12:57,420 --> 00:12:59,250
只有一个迷你小环岛。
There's only a mini round about.

296
00:12:59,250 --> 00:13:00,570
<i>右转开上乔治榆树巷。</i>
<i>Turn right up Georges Elm Lane.</i>

297
00:13:00,570 --> 00:13:02,970
<i>乔治榆树巷，也就是右边第一个路口。</i>
<i>Georges Elm Lane, which is the first on the right.</i>

298
00:13:02,970 --> 00:13:04,450
穿过工业园区。
Pass industrial estate.

299
00:13:09,420 --> 00:13:12,250
到了这个阶段，局势已经相当不妙了。
At this stage, things were going quite badly.

300
00:13:12,250 --> 00:13:15,970
于是我们把卡车和刨路机交给了专业人士。
So we handed the lorry and the plainer over to the professionals.

301
00:13:15,970 --> 00:13:19,350
理查德被分派去干清理现场这种简单活，
Richard was then given the simple job of tidying up,

302
00:13:19,350 --> 00:13:23,170
而我则回去继续做战前动员演讲。
and I went back to making motivational speeches.

303
00:13:23,670 --> 00:13:26,320
这绝非终点，
This is not the end,

304
00:13:26,320 --> 00:13:28,820
这也不是起点，
this is not the beginning,

305
00:13:28,820 --> 00:13:32,250
这甚至不是终点的起点，
this is not the beginning of the end,

306
00:13:32,250 --> 00:13:33,550
它甚至都不算……
it's not even...

307
00:13:33,550 --> 00:13:35,520
在工人们被“充分激励”之后，
With the men motivated nicely,

308
00:13:35,520 --> 00:13:37,270
我们很快就把旧路面清理干净了，
we soon have the old surface cleared

309
00:13:37,270 --> 00:13:41,300
随后开始浇洒沥青粘层，用来固定新铺的沥青路面。
and then started to lay the bitumen which glues the new tarmac in place.

310
00:13:42,400 --> 00:13:45,150
接着有人开始问能不能休息一下。
Some people then began to ask if they could have a break.

311
00:13:45,150 --> 00:13:47,400
答案当然是：没门。
But of course the answer was no.

312
00:13:48,800 --> 00:13:51,250
我们就是靠这个把进度赶上来的。
This is how we're managing to speed things up.

313
00:13:51,850 --> 00:13:55,720
在这个工地上，树篱里能揪到什么，午饭就吃什么。
Lunch on this job is what you can find in the hedge.

314
00:13:56,650 --> 00:14:01,270
不过，单靠狄更斯时代的残酷剥削，可没法在一天之内把活干完。
Dickensian work practices alone though, would not get this job done in a day.

315
00:14:01,270 --> 00:14:03,850
你还得往里疯狂砸资源，
You also need to throw resources at it.

316
00:14:03,850 --> 00:14:07,170
而这正是市政部门死活都不愿意做的事。
something councils seem unwilling to do.

