00:36:57,205 --> 00:37:01,069
<i>收音机：我想用我的余生，好好爱你。</i>
<i>I want the chance to spend the rest of my life, loving you.</i>

786
00:37:01,484 --> 00:37:05,670
天呐，斯提格似乎迷上了言情小说的有声书光盘。
Oh dear, the Stig seems to have developed a taste for romantic fiction on CD.

787
00:37:06,111 --> 00:37:09,147
好，通过芝加哥弯，跟开卡丁车一样甩来甩去。
OK, he's through Chicago, sliding around like a go-cart.

788
00:37:09,231 --> 00:37:10,502
现在进锤头弯了。
Here he is coming into Hammerhead.

789
00:37:11,061 --> 00:37:13,211
到处都是融雪汇成的积水。
Plagues of melted snow every where.

790
00:37:13,253 --> 00:37:15,768
会出现推头吗？一点都没有，瞧瞧这走位！
Is he gonna understeer? Not a bit of it. Look at that!

791
00:37:15,776 --> 00:37:18,367
你看，没有哪辆车漂移起来能像它这么顺。
You see there is no car that drifts like this one.

792
00:37:20,838 --> 00:37:22,144
车尾都在水上漂了。
With the backward plaining.

793
00:37:22,398 --> 00:37:26,445
<i>收音机：还有她那位金发红颜的阿喀琉斯……</i>
<i>Radio: With her own golden haired ruddy faced Archilles</i>

794
00:37:27,257 --> 00:37:29,060
现在真是油门踩到底了。
He's really got the hammer down now.

795
00:37:29,060 --> 00:37:32,802
你能看到车身在积水上剧烈晃动，斯提格却面不改色。
you see the car twitching over the standing water. Stig isn't faced.

796
00:37:33,214 --> 00:37:35,762
或许是因为他老家母星就是片大沼泽吧。
Maybe it's 'cause his home planet is quite swampy.

797
00:37:36,101 --> 00:37:37,764
呃……进入倒数第二个弯，
Err¡­penultimate to the corner,

798
00:37:38,120 --> 00:37:40,279
碾过了草地，现在来到甘邦弯，
dips into the grass, Gambon now,

799
00:37:40,304 --> 00:37:43,354
大力切入，一把把车横甩过去，
hard in, chucks it side ways

800
00:37:43,667 --> 00:37:45,572
冲线！
and across the line!

801
00:37:47,436 --> 00:37:47,766
那么
Now

802
00:37:50,174 --> 00:37:51,258
他的成绩是……
he did it...

803
00:37:52,432 --> 00:37:54,743
1分34秒7，
in 1:34.7,

804
00:37:54,751 --> 00:37:58,705
这显然惨不忍睹，但我觉得当时赛道确实非常、非常、非常湿滑。
which is obvious pathetic, but I think it was really very very very wet.

805
00:37:58,739 --> 00:38:00,652
呃……我们本来还打算随后让阿斯顿也去跑一圈的，
Err.. we were gonna put the Aston round afterwards,

806
00:38:00,660 --> 00:38:02,582
结果又开始下雪了，所以别怪我们
but it started to snow again, so don't blame us

807
00:38:02,607 --> 00:38:03,572
呃……因为我们根本懒得去折腾，
Err... 'cause we didn't bother,

808
00:38:03,801 --> 00:38:05,672
也别怪斯提格，学学其他人——
don't blame the Stig do what every one else does.

809
00:38:05,994 --> 00:38:07,273
统统甩锅给全球变暖就成了。
And just blame Global Warming.

810
00:38:08,949 --> 00:38:11,268
此前，我们出发执行一项任务，
Now earlier on we set out on a mission

811
00:38:11,268 --> 00:38:14,519
旨在证明修路根本用不着拖那么久。
to demonstrate that roadworks needn't take so long

812
00:38:14,824 --> 00:38:21,410
沃里克郡议会估计，重铺D5481公路一段1.5英里的路面得花上整整5天。
Warwickshire council reckoned it will take 5 days to resurface a 1.5 mile stretch of the D5481.

813
00:38:21,876 --> 00:38:26,100
但我们觉得，只要埋头苦干，别被那些繁文缛节的“健康与安全规范”捆住手脚，
But we reckoned, by working hard, and not get all tangled up in Health and Safty

814
00:38:26,278 --> 00:38:28,564
我们区区24小时就能搞定。
We could do it in just 24 hours

815
00:38:29,023 --> 00:38:31,953
在上一段节目告一段落时，我感觉进展其实相当顺利。
And when we left the action it was going really rather well I thought.

816
00:38:31,995 --> 00:38:35,872
这边的哈蒙德在采石场，确保源源不断地送来新鲜沥青，
Hammond here was down at the quarry keeping up a steady stream of fresh tarmac

817
00:38:36,193 --> 00:38:38,546
我开着摊铺机在路上摊铺，
I was driving a paver laying it on the road

818
00:38:38,572 --> 00:38:41,456
而杰里米则肩负着至关重要的重任——
and Jeremy was fulfilling the vital role

819
00:38:41,507 --> 00:38:43,844
拿着大喇叭冲所有人大呼小叫。
of shouting at everyone down a megaphone.

820
00:38:50,223 --> 00:38:51,538
快点！给我使劲干！
Come on! Put it back into it.

821
00:38:51,563 --> 00:38:53,299
你，伙计，过来，我给你示范一下。
You, man, here, let me show you.

822
00:38:54,585 --> 00:38:57,413
但紧接着，一切突然全乱套了。
But then all of a sudden everything went wrong.

823
00:38:58,860 --> 00:38:59,961
沥青用光了！
Run out of tarmac!

824
00:39:00,582 --> 00:39:01,759
什么叫用光了？
What do you mean you've run out?

825
00:39:01,962 --> 00:39:03,495
因为哈蒙德的货车还没到。
For Hammonds lorry's not here.

826
00:39:03,613 --> 00:39:04,987
我们一共需要一千吨。
We need a thousand tons.

827
00:39:05,351 --> 00:39:08,111
而他那一卡车拉来的，只够铺眼前那一小截。
And his lorry load only does that little stretch there.

828
00:39:08,475 --> 00:39:09,982
要是他不能尽快送过来，
And if he doesn't get it here quick enough

829
00:39:09,982 --> 00:39:12,497
那层沥青黏合剂就会硬化失效，粘不牢了。
that bitumen stuff goes off and it won't stick.

830
00:39:13,157 --> 00:39:14,890
<i>哈蒙德，我们断料了！</i>
<i>Hammond we're out!</i>

831
00:39:15,330 --> 00:39:16,325
我们才铺了100英尺。
We've done 100 feet.

832
00:39:16,325 --> 00:39:18,636
<i> 你到底搞了几辆卡车在运？</i>
<i> How many trucks have you got working on this?</i>

833
00:39:18,636 --> 00:39:19,911
我们这儿现在有三辆，
We've got three in here now

834
00:39:19,911 --> 00:39:22,772
我能看见一辆正在装货，一辆在地磅上过磅。
We've got one be loaded one on the way bridge that I can see.

835
00:39:22,772 --> 00:39:24,559
<i> 而且我……我这儿根本塞不下更多卡车了。</i>
<i> And I am... I can't get anymore in it.</i>

836
00:39:24,694 --> 00:39:26,667
你总共才弄来五辆卡车？行吧。
You've only got five trucks? Right.

837
00:39:26,701 --> 00:39:29,240
<i> 今天附近还有别的地方在修路吗？</i>
<i> Are there any other roadwork's going on today?</i>

838
00:39:30,502 --> 00:39:32,585
<i>- 干嘛？去顺走人家的沥青？
- 没错。</i>
<i>- What? That we can nick their tarmac?
- Yeah.</i>

839
00:39:33,890 --> 00:39:35,955
我喜欢你这主意，够损的。
I like your thinking there. that's quite devious.

840
00:39:36,243 --> 00:39:37,572
<i> 去截胡他们的沥青。</i>
<i> Nick their tarmac.</i>

841
00:39:37,820 --> 00:39:39,454
你下一趟活，知道是要送去哪儿吗？
Your next job, do you know where it's going?

842
00:39:39,809 --> 00:39:41,561
是要送到……你看，那根本不是我们要修的路！
Is it going to... You see that's not our road

843
00:39:41,561 --> 00:39:43,237
那有个屁用！送我们那儿去！
Well that's useless. Send it to us.

844
00:39:43,390 --> 00:39:45,786
千万别给他们送，是我们需要料！
Just don't send it to them. We need it.

845
00:39:46,170 --> 00:39:48,294
赶紧火力全开！还有，把那挂历给我换了。
Crack now to the max. And change that calendar.

846
00:39:48,294 --> 00:39:49,903
看着未免也太安逸祥和了。
It's far too calming and relaxing.

847
00:39:53,734 --> 00:39:56,451
动起来！快点！走啊！
Move! Come on! Go!

848
00:39:56,477 --> 00:39:58,568
搞快点，麻溜点干！
Fast, Get on with it!

849
00:39:59,076 --> 00:40:00,261
哈哈，又装好一辆！
Hahahh, another one.

850
00:40:00,269 --> 00:40:01,288
我直接挥舞起小皮鞭，
I cracked the whip

851
00:40:01,406 --> 00:40:03,726
甚至还推出了一套奖励方案。
and even introduced an incentive scheme.

852
00:40:03,726 --> 00:40:05,928
我要你开得跟一阵风一样快，明白吗？
I want you to go like the wind, OK?

853
00:40:06,258 --> 00:40:08,197
超速罚单全都由我来掏！
I'll pay you speeding fines.

854
00:40:09,148 --> 00:40:12,280
但残酷的现实是，采石场离这儿足足有一小时车程。
But the fact remained that the quarry was an hour away.

855
00:40:12,288 --> 00:40:14,092
而且哈蒙德手里总共就只有五辆卡车。
And Hammond only had five trucks.

856
00:40:14,252 --> 00:40:15,819
这根本不够用。
That wasn't enough.

857
00:40:17,093 --> 00:40:20,721
修路之所以总要拖拖拉拉耗很久，
The main reason why roadworks take a long time

858
00:40:21,356 --> 00:40:24,684
最主要的原因就是运料卡车送得根本不够连贯。
is because the trucks just don't come regularly enough.

859
00:40:24,684 --> 00:40:26,944
- 那个跟你……一起干活的工人。
- 对。
- That guy that... you're working with.
- Yeah.

860
00:40:27,147 --> 00:40:28,991
他说他干这行已经干了32年，
He said he's worked till the way it is now for 32 years

861
00:40:28,991 --> 00:40:31,539
其中有24年都在原地杵着等卡车。
24 of which has been standing around waiting for the trucks.

862
00:40:31,827 --> 00:40:32,907
我们早就跟哈蒙德挑明了这事。
We told Hammond this.

863
00:40:33,085 --> 00:40:36,776
我们对哈蒙德千叮万嘱：唯一重要的事情，就是让卡车源源不断地送过来。
We said to Hammond it's the only important thing: keep the trucks coming.

864
00:40:37,801 --> 00:40:40,138
沥青确实还在陆陆续续地送过来，
The tarmac did continued to dribbled in,

865
00:40:40,138 --> 00:40:41,856
但简直慢得令人发指。而就在这时——
but far too slowly, and then

866
00:40:42,085 --> 00:40:43,075
视线转回采石场……
Back at the quarry

867
00:40:45,024 --> 00:40:46,370
怎么停工了？机器怎么停了？！
What's killed it? Why is it stopped?

868
00:40:46,396 --> 00:40:47,293
按了急停。
Emergency stop.

869
00:40:47,437 --> 00:40:49,100
好端端的按什么急停？！又没……
Why is it in the emergency stop? There is no...

870
00:40:49,362 --> 00:40:50,895
谁靠上去了？我们靠到什么了？
Who's lent, we've lent on the what?

871
00:40:51,580 --> 00:40:52,786
- 谁干的……
- 你的人。
- Who's...
- Your man.

872
00:40:52,845 --> 00:40:55,376
摄像师靠……我们靠到了那个紧急……
The camera man lent... we lent on the emergency...

873
00:40:56,902 --> 00:40:57,960
你把整座搅拌站都给停了？！
You stopped the plant?

874
00:40:58,883 --> 00:41:00,974
<i>对，我们……呃，好像稍微碰到了急停开关。</i>
<i>Yeah, we sort of hit the emergency stop a bit.</i>

875
00:41:03,125 --> 00:41:03,972
你碰那玩意儿干什么？！
Why have you done that?

876
00:41:04,116 --> 00:41:05,267
<i>这纯属一场该死的意外，好吗！</i>
<i> Well this was a bloody accident, wasn't it.</i>

877
00:41:05,267 --> 00:41:06,994
<i>我又不是故意的！</i>
<i> I didn't do it on purpose.</i>

878
00:41:07,316 --> 00:41:09,008
理查德，理查德，理查德……
Richard, Richard, Richard

879
00:41:09,152 --> 00:41:12,038
我给你提个真诚的建议：别回这儿来了。
I'm gonna make a suggestion: Don't come back here.

880
00:41:12,690 --> 00:41:13,977
千万……千万别回来。
Don't... don't come back,

881
00:41:14,095 --> 00:41:16,339
滚开，滚去火地……
go away, go to Tierra del...

882
00:41:16,567 --> 00:41:20,597
火地岛去吧，就算逃到那儿我也照样追杀过去弄死你。
Tierra del Fuego, and even I'm gonna hunt you down and kill you there as well.

883
00:41:23,727 --> 00:41:25,895
D5481公路上的弟兄们！
Men at the D5481

884
00:41:27,636 --> 00:41:29,820
这是我们最黑暗的时刻
This is our darkest hour

885
00:41:30,591 --> 00:41:33,833
我们绝不容许阿道夫·哈蒙德
We will not allow Adolf Hammond

886
00:41:34,112 --> 00:41:38,667
破坏我们这伟大、这精彩、这壮丽的……
to ruin our plans for this great, this wonderful, this magnificent...

887
00:41:39,556 --> 00:41:40,165
闭嘴！
Shut up!

888
00:41:42,324 --> 00:41:44,298
我们把那个劳保安监员给埋了
We buried the Health and Safety man

889
00:41:44,298 --> 00:41:46,939
边等采石场重新恢复供料。
While we waited for the quarry to restart.

890
00:41:47,752 --> 00:41:48,539
结果人家压根没开
But it didn't

891
00:41:48,556 --> 00:41:50,707
当时已经五点整，到下班的点了。
It was five o'clock, knocking-off time.

892
00:41:51,613 --> 00:41:52,900
工人们全都各回各家了。
And they'd all gone home.

893
00:41:53,462 --> 00:41:55,367
机器我们全关了，那个……
We've shut down the plant, that...

894
00:41:55,376 --> 00:41:56,612
就到这了，我们不能再干了。
That's it. We can't work anymore.

895
00:41:57,340 --> 00:41:59,437
呵，你们那些哥们每周只上35小时班
Well, your friends're on a 35-hour week

896
00:42:00,114 --> 00:42:02,104
换做大部分工程，这时候早撂挑子了。
Most jobs would stop at this point.

897
00:42:02,159 --> 00:42:06,691
但我们充分发挥主观能动性，找了家通宵营业的新采石场。
But we used our initiative and found a new quarry that would stay open through the night.

898
00:42:07,284 --> 00:42:08,579
在哪儿？这家新的？
Where is it? This new one?

899
00:42:09,187 --> 00:42:11,270
<i>- 阿什伯恩
- 阿什伯恩？</i>
<i>- Ashbourne
- Ashbourne?</i>

900
00:42:11,312 --> 00:42:13,357
- 那是在肯特郡。
- 在德比郡。
- That's in Kent.
- In Derbyshire.

901
00:42:13,357 --> 00:42:14,718
要是我开着另一台机器去阿什伯恩呢？
If I go over to Ashbourne with the other plant?

902
00:42:14,718 --> 00:42:17,469
别去阿什伯恩，你离任何采石场都远点儿。
Don't go to Ashbourne, don't go anywhere near a quarry.

903
00:42:17,704 --> 00:42:18,805
全被你搅黄了。
You're ruining it.

904
00:42:19,118 --> 00:42:21,708
紧接着，就在我们刚稳住局面的当口。
And then just as we were getting on top of things.

905
00:42:23,911 --> 00:42:27,202
用鲍兹尔·弗尔蒂的名言来说：“哦，太特么妙了！”
In the immortal words of Basil Fawlty: "Oh spiffing!"

906
00:42:29,606 --> 00:42:32,598
要是暴风雨真砸下来，运来多少沥青都白搭。
If a storm broke it wouldn't matter how much tarmac came.

907
00:42:32,598 --> 00:42:34,088
因为我们根本没法铺。
'Cause we wouldn't be able to lay it.

908
00:42:34,723 --> 00:42:36,611
很显然，这时候必须来段演讲了。
Plainly, a speech was in order.

909
00:42:37,220 --> 00:42:40,028
我们绝不会悄无声息地步入良夜。
We shall not go quietly into the night.

910
00:42:41,044 --> 00:42:43,496
白班我们历经了重重波折，但是……
We are faced diversity in the day shift, but...

911
00:42:59,240 --> 00:43:01,264
夜幕降临，大雨倾盆而下。
As night fell, the rain came.

912
00:43:01,425 --> 00:43:04,094
换成普通的修路工地，到这就该歇菜了。
And in a normal roadworks that would be that.

913
00:43:05,279 --> 00:43:07,233
但我坚决不许任何人停工
But I refused to let anyone stop

914
00:43:07,326 --> 00:43:10,382
因为第二家采石场的料刚好送到。
Because the second quarry had just started to deliver.

915
00:43:10,804 --> 00:43:13,200
这场面看着真叫人心里舒坦。
This is a sight to warm the cockles of your heart.

916
00:43:13,514 --> 00:43:15,572
- 妙极了。
- 工人们通宵奋战。
- Marvelous.
- Men working at night.

917
00:43:15,572 --> 00:43:18,518
总听人吹嘘说：“我去过日本，人家都是连夜赶工。”
You're always hearing people say that 'I went to Japan and they work through the night.'

918
00:43:18,518 --> 00:43:20,881
“我去过瑞士，人家也是连夜赶工。”
'I went to Switzerland, they work through the night.'

919
00:43:21,491 --> 00:43:24,009
看看咱们大英帝国，咱们也在连夜赶工！
Here we are in England and we're working through the night.

920
00:43:25,710 --> 00:43:29,080
为了确保彼得福德的乡亲们能早日通车
And to make sure that people of Bidford got their work done quickly

921
00:43:29,173 --> 00:43:31,358
晚饭休息时间我们也没闲着。
We've been working through our supper break as well.

922
00:43:33,627 --> 00:43:36,387
给我来75份炸鳕鱼配薯条。
Can I have Cod and chips, 75 times

923
00:43:52,042 --> 00:43:54,489
- 再加一根面糊炸香肠。
- 好的，多谢。
- And a butter sausage.
- Yes, thank you.

924
00:43:59,748 --> 00:44:01,179
- 薯条来喽！
- 嗷！
- Chips!
- Ohh!

925
00:44:01,179 --> 00:44:03,287
别光顾着抢，得我来发，我有活儿交给你。
Yeah, but don't just grab them, I got to hand them out, I got a job for you.

926
00:44:03,287 --> 00:44:04,861
- 你能去把湿巾发一下吗？
- 没问题。
- Can you hand out the wipes?
- Yeah.

927
00:44:05,225 --> 00:44:07,248
- 大伙儿肯定会……
- 给你。
- That'll appreciate...
- There you go.

928
00:44:07,282 --> 00:44:08,868
趁理查德去买晚饭，
While Richard was getting supper,

929
00:44:08,910 --> 00:44:13,328
我装了另一个“激励神器”，好给大家鼓鼓劲。
I'd installed another motivational tool to keep everyone spirits up.

930
00:44:13,896 --> 00:44:17,159
夜黑风高，长路漫漫。
The night is dark, the road is long.

931
00:44:17,303 --> 00:44:19,436
我们远离家室。
And we are far from our families.

932
00:44:19,888 --> 00:44:20,836
但别担心，
But don't worry,

933
00:44:21,200 --> 00:44:24,088
D5481公路上的纯爷们儿们，
Gentlemen at D5481,

934
00:44:24,257 --> 00:44:27,335
因为我有音乐陪我们熬过漫漫长夜！
Because I have music to take us through the night!

935
00:44:28,123 --> 00:44:29,392
燥起来吧！
Chech it out!

936
00:44:32,257 --> 00:44:33,831
恶心得我香肠都吃不下了。
It's put me off the sausage.

937
00:44:40,275 --> 00:44:41,392
一比一平了，詹姆斯。
/One-all, James.

938
00:44:43,946 --> 00:44:45,791
这才叫修路嘛！
This is how you run roadworks

939
00:44:45,800 --> 00:44:47,797
美味的炸鱼薯条，动感的音乐，
Good fish and chips, good music

940
00:44:47,873 --> 00:44:49,812
彻底告别狗屁安全与健康规范。
No Health and no Safty.

941
00:44:50,235 --> 00:44:53,087
我觉得这绝对是此时此刻全英国……
I just think that this is the happiest roadwork crew

942
00:44:53,146 --> 00:44:55,858
干活最开心的施工队了。
working in the land right now anywhere.

943
00:44:56,484 --> 00:44:59,845
大伙儿也很乐见领导能卷起袖子一起干。
The guys also like the willingness of the bosses to muck in.

944
00:45:00,031 --> 00:45:03,570
想到这里，詹姆斯和理查德接管了压路机。
And with that in mind, James and Richard took over the roller.

945
00:45:03,663 --> 00:45:05,754
你得压住这个边缘一点。
You've got to, just overlap the edge of this.

946
00:45:05,754 --> 00:45:08,879
如果我开得太靠边，直接陷进草地里，那你就得……
If I go too far over the edge just stick it in the verge, and then you've got to..

947
00:45:08,879 --> 00:45:10,538
不，老天，该死！
No, God, bugger

948
00:45:11,020 --> 00:45:13,112
你把水阀给碾了，你个大白痴！
You've run over the stop cock you cock.

949
00:45:13,188 --> 00:45:14,296
我都听到哐当一声了。
I heard it go clanging.

950
00:45:14,973 --> 00:45:16,776
喔，太糟了，我们要大祸临头了。
Woo, that's bad, we are gonna in trouble.

951
00:45:16,790 --> 00:45:18,339
这事儿我们该跟谁坦白啊？
Who are we gonna tell about this?

952
00:45:18,678 --> 00:45:21,819
啊，这样，我们可以开着压路机……
Ahh. Well, what we could do is take steamroller.

953
00:45:23,433 --> 00:45:24,796
- 直接继续往前开？
- 没错。
- And just keep going?
- Yeah.

954
00:45:30,614 --> 00:45:34,458
凌晨四点，还剩下700码没铺完。
At 4 am, there were still 700 yards to go.

955
00:45:34,466 --> 00:45:36,202
工人们都快累趴下了。
And the men were flagging.

956
00:45:37,438 --> 00:45:41,195
于是，我祭出了激励士气的终极大杀器。
So, I brought out the motivational big gun

957
00:45:41,195 --> 00:45:43,488
……又一个“不满的冬日”？
... another Winter of discontent?

958
00:45:44,013 --> 00:45:46,002
这是……撒切尔夫人。
This is... Mrs Thatcher

959
00:45:46,900 --> 00:45:48,229
- 没错。
- 用来激励大伙儿。
- Yeah.
- To motivate the men.

960
00:45:49,491 --> 00:45:50,354
效果拔群啊。
This is going well.

961
00:45:51,079 --> 00:45:55,439
希望接下来能迎来一个讲常识的寒冬。
And I hope it will be followed by a Winter of common sense.

962
00:45:55,531 --> 00:45:58,020
妙啊，这句我喜欢。
Yes, I like that one.

963
00:45:58,036 --> 00:45:59,688
别助长他的歪风，伙计，这也太……
Don't encourage him, man, this is...

964
00:45:59,688 --> 00:46:02,795
不过工友们可不像詹姆斯那样天天看《每日电讯报》，
The chaps however were not telegraph readers like James

965
00:46:02,804 --> 00:46:07,301
所以我向他们保证：铺得越快，我就越早把这玩意儿关了。
So I promised them that the sooner they finish the laying the sooner I'll switch her off.

966
00:46:10,297 --> 00:46:13,511
这招果然灵验，破晓前路面就重新铺好了。
That worked, and by day break the road was resurfaced

967
00:46:13,993 --> 00:46:17,080
但留给我们的时间，只够狼吞虎咽一顿快手早餐。
But there were still only time for a quick power breakfast.

968
00:46:17,910 --> 00:46:19,579
流浪汉干嘛非得窝在伦敦呢？
Why do tramps live in London?

969
00:46:20,197 --> 00:46:21,509
- 明明乡下有这么大片好风光。
- 就是啊。
- When there is all this out here.
- Yeah.

970
00:46:24,548 --> 00:46:28,823
我们向比德福德的居民承诺过，早上9点07分就把路还给他们，
We'd promised the people of Bidford they'd have their road back by 9:07

971
00:46:28,831 --> 00:46:30,270
可手头还有一大堆事没干。
And there was still much to do

972
00:46:30,703 --> 00:46:32,134
施工设备得清理撤走，
The plants needed clearing

973
00:46:32,142 --> 00:46:34,191
哈蒙德得把路标重新立起来，
Hammond needed to get the signs back up.

974
00:46:34,640 --> 00:46:37,266
我和詹姆斯还得在路面上画白线。
And James and I had the white lines to paint.

975
00:46:37,596 --> 00:46:40,048
看，就差那么一丁点儿，还行吧？
Look, that's a little bit, OK?

976
00:46:41,623 --> 00:46:43,283
- 堪称完美。
- 才怪。
- That perfect.
- It isn't.

977
00:46:44,240 --> 00:46:46,280
哈哈哈哈……
Hahhaha..

978
00:46:47,305 --> 00:46:48,262
我们确实尽力了，
We did our best,

979
00:46:48,295 --> 00:46:51,097
但市政局来的那帮人似乎并不买账。
but the men from the council didn't seem impressed.

980
00:46:51,732 --> 00:46:56,218
嘿哈哈哈……
Hehahaha..

981
00:46:56,814 --> 00:47:00,238
白线被我们画得一塌糊涂，眼看着时间一分一秒过去，
We had made a terrible mess of the lines and with the clock ticking

982
00:47:00,365 --> 00:47:02,008
我们赶紧跑去找哈蒙德，
we ram to see Hammond,

983
00:47:02,397 --> 00:47:05,174
结果发现他的路标立得更是一团糟。
who've made a even bigger mess with his signs.

984
00:47:05,284 --> 00:47:06,164
斜坡明明在那边，
The hill is there,

985
00:47:07,519 --> 00:47:09,382
而且那是……车是朝那个方向开的。
And that's... you're going that way.

986
00:47:10,161 --> 00:47:11,312
标牌应该朝向那边才对。
They should be facing that way.

987
00:47:11,719 --> 00:47:14,749
你说得对，我这等于是在提醒大家：你们刚刚拐了几个急弯，
You're right, I'm just telling people they've just been around some bends.

988
00:47:14,766 --> 00:47:16,155
- 外加刚下了一个坡。
- 走开，别烦我。
- And down a hill.
- Go away, leave me lone.

989
00:47:16,214 --> 00:47:16,696
行吧。
Alright.

990
00:47:17,213 --> 00:47:19,391
事实证明，他把所有牌子全都装反了。
As it turned out, he's done them all wrong.

991
00:47:19,416 --> 00:47:22,515
而我们只剩整整十分钟来把它们复原。
And we had just ten minutes to put them right.

992
00:47:22,515 --> 00:47:23,491
噢，真见鬼！
Oh, bloody hell!

993
00:47:23,516 --> 00:47:25,319
- 这一堆全是你装的？  - 是啊。
- 好，退后。
- Did you do this stuff?  - Yeah.
- Right, stand back.

994
00:47:25,641 --> 00:47:26,388
你到底是怎么做到的……
How did you do it...

995
00:47:27,540 --> 00:47:28,920
- 搞定，完美！
- 成了，大功告成！
- There you go. Perfect.
- There. That's it, finished.

996
00:47:29,004 --> 00:47:30,240
- 开放道路！
- 走起！
- Open road!
- Right.

997
00:47:32,836 --> 00:47:34,867
这事儿我早就想干一次了。
I've been wanting to do this for a long time.

998
00:47:36,108 --> 00:47:36,802
噢，快点啊！
Oh, come on!

999
00:47:37,217 --> 00:47:38,444
来啦来啦！
I'm coming.

1000
00:47:39,217 --> 00:47:41,293
整天就数你嚎得最大声。
You're the one who's been shouting all day.

1001
00:47:41,506 --> 00:47:47,084
瞧好了，比德福德-埃文的乡亲们，不到一天工夫，
So there you are. People of Bidford-on-Avon in just under one day,

1002
00:47:47,973 --> 00:47:49,031
你们的路通了。
your road is open.

1003
00:47:49,886 --> 00:47:51,232
乐意为您效劳。
Glad to be of service.

1004
00:48:02,220 --> 00:48:05,168
如果我们能搞定……如果我们都能搞定，
If we can do that... If we can do that.

1005
00:48:05,414 --> 00:48:06,565
那帮修路的没理由搞不定。
They should be able to do that.

1006
00:48:06,565 --> 00:48:09,782
讲真，我们还真有几条《Top Gear》修路锦囊送给建筑施工界。
Really we do have some Top Gear top tips here for the construction industry.

1007
00:48:10,369 --> 00:48:11,581
手脚麻利点，
Work fast,

1008
00:48:12,038 --> 00:48:13,139
多吃黑莓，
Eat blackberries

1009
00:48:13,537 --> 00:48:16,187
叫上一百辆卡车，别就叫五辆。
Get 100 trucks, not 5.

1010
00:48:16,280 --> 00:48:19,011
对，再给那台铺路机装个涡轮增压。
Yeah, and fit that paving machine thing with a turbo charger

1011
00:48:19,028 --> 00:48:20,907
- 对，还有千万别让他去开。
- 千万别，可别那么干。
- Yeah, and don't let him drive it
- No, don't do that.

1012
00:48:21,285 --> 00:48:24,425
行了，接下来，就是大家
Anyway, now, it's the moment

1013
00:48:24,713 --> 00:48:25,771
翘首以盼的时刻了。
you've all been waiting for.

1014
00:48:27,151 --> 00:48:29,775
达维娜正在《老大哥》那边现场直播呢，
Devena is live on state of the Big Brother.

1015
00:48:30,156 --> 00:48:32,560
总冠军马上就要揭晓了。
winner is about to be announced.

1016
00:48:33,356 --> 00:48:35,948
不过在我们BBC二台，我们要看我们这小矮个撞车。
Here on BBC2 however we got our little fella's car crash

1017
00:48:35,999 --> 00:48:37,235
来吧老兄，给我们讲讲当时的情况。
So come on mate, talk us through it.

1018
00:48:37,334 --> 00:48:39,552
行吧。瞧，这有些我们自己都没看过的录像。
Oh Ok. Well, and look, we got some video of it we never looked.

1019
00:48:39,561 --> 00:48:41,559
这是……出事前拍的。
Here is umm.. Here's before it happened.

1020
00:48:41,576 --> 00:48:44,134
就是这辆车，叫“吸血鬼”（Vampire）。
This is the car. It's called the Vampire.

1021
00:48:44,329 --> 00:48:49,133
基本上它就是台硕大无比的喷气发动机，前头用螺栓固定了把椅子，仅此而已。
Basically it's just a socking great jet engine with a chair bolted to the front of it.That's it.

1022
00:48:49,573 --> 00:48:50,724
那这玩意儿算高科技吗？
So is it high tech?

1023
00:48:51,029 --> 00:48:51,867
算，相当高科技。
Yes, it's fairly high tech.

1024
00:48:51,876 --> 00:48:54,178
那台发动机，喷气发动机，是从“红箭”飞行表演队军机上拆下来的。
The engine, the jet engine, comes out of a Red Arrow.

1025
00:48:54,601 --> 00:48:57,759
转向机来自一辆信赖知更鸟（Reliant Robin）。
The steering box is from a Reliant Robin.

1026
00:48:58,256 --> 00:49:00,169
燃油泵是从水泥搅拌机上拆的。
And the fuel pumps from a cement mixer.

1027
00:49:02,075 --> 00:49:04,174
哦，这就是我本来要开着它飙车的机场。
Oh, that's the airfield where I was gonna be driving it.

1028
00:49:04,191 --> 00:49:06,765
- 瞧，在约克郡附近的埃尔文顿。
- 哎呀，这车复杂得很。
- See, that's in Elvington near York.
- Oh, it's complicated.

1029
00:49:07,906 --> 00:49:13,365
当然了，在这种跑道上搞这种极限狂飙，你最不想要的一样东西……
There is of course one thing you really don't want when you're doing this sort of stuff up a runway.

1030
00:49:13,713 --> 00:49:15,550
就像吹成那样。侧风。
Like that one. Cross winds.

1031
00:49:18,792 --> 00:49:20,067
是啊，当时风确实有点大。
Yeah, there was a bit of breeze.

1032
00:49:20,076 --> 00:49:21,693
哦，看，那会儿我正钻进去呢。
Oh that was me getting in it, you see.

1033
00:49:21,848 --> 00:49:22,728
就在那儿，然后……
At there and...

1034
00:49:23,101 --> 00:49:25,649
造车的老哥正在给我做安全简报。
And then I got a briefing from the man who built it.

1035
00:49:26,026 --> 00:49:28,693
所以我今天的挑战就是开这玩意儿，
So my challenge today is to drive this thing,

1036
00:49:29,447 --> 00:49:32,377
不过，这还不是全部。
except, that's not the full story

1037
00:49:32,631 --> 00:49:37,754
因为我今天的挑战不仅是开它，还得按下这个看着人畜无害的小按钮。
Because my challenge today is to drive this thing and hit this innocent-looking little button.

1038
00:49:38,254 --> 00:49:41,785
因为一旦按下去，就会有一道火柱喷射穿过发动机，
Because when I do that, it sends a flame, shooting through the engine

1039
00:49:42,005 --> 00:49:43,413
进而点燃加力燃烧室。
which ignites the afterburner.

1040
00:49:43,794 --> 00:49:46,808
到了那一刻，我拥有的可就不止是五千匹马力了……
And when that happens I haven't got 5,000 horse power,

1041
00:49:47,244 --> 00:49:49,860
我有……一万匹马力，
I've got, 10,000 horse power,

1042
00:49:50,410 --> 00:49:53,974
我也许会是你们这辈子见过的最大的车祸现场。
I'm possibly the biggest accident, you've ever seen in your life.

1043
00:49:58,567 --> 00:50:00,134
我敢说你当时讲这话的时候，
I bet when you said that,

1044
00:50:00,150 --> 00:50:01,573
心里肯定觉得自己特……
it was one of those...

1045
00:50:03,746 --> 00:50:04,355
帅吧！
Yeah!

1046
00:50:06,355 --> 00:50:08,700
太丢人了，真够丢人的。
Pathetic, very pathetic.

1047
00:50:10,613 --> 00:50:12,213
而且我敢打赌，你说这话时肯定在琢磨：
And I bet when you said that you thought

1048
00:50:12,230 --> 00:50:16,380
“来句俏皮话，显得这事儿比实际情况更要命一点”。
it's one of those snappy lines to make this look a bit more dangerous than it really is.

1049
00:50:16,414 --> 00:50:18,844
说出口的时候我还真是这么想的。
It's exactly what I thought when I said it.

1050
00:50:18,886 --> 00:50:20,959
我能问清楚一点吗？这玩意是不是……
Can I just qualify something about it? Is it...

1051
00:50:21,120 --> 00:50:23,360
它其实没有传统意义上的油门踏板？
It doesn't have like a throttle in the accelerator.

1052
00:50:23,394 --> 00:50:25,485
- 不像普通车那样。
- 对，这是喷气车。开起来完全是两码事。
- Like a normal car.
- No, a jet car. No, it is complete different to drive.

1053
00:50:25,519 --> 00:50:27,319
它根本没有离合器之类的玩意儿。
There is no clutches or such.

1054
00:50:27,345 --> 00:50:29,259
你只要拧中控台上的旋钮，把发动机调到你想要的输出就行。
You just turn the engine up to what you want with the knob on the dash.

1055
00:50:29,259 --> 00:50:30,351
而且是在起步之前调。
That's before you set off.

1056
00:50:30,377 --> 00:50:31,875
对，启动时调好，之后就别管了。
Yeah, you do that when you start it, you leave it.

1057
00:50:31,892 --> 00:50:33,018
所以根本没有油门踏板。
So there is no accelerator.

1058
00:50:33,027 --> 00:50:35,058
你只要把脚从脚刹上挪开，车就开拔了。
You pull away by just taking you foot off the footbrake.

1059
00:50:35,084 --> 00:50:36,100
之后就不用再碰刹车了。
You don't touch that again.

1060
00:50:36,287 --> 00:50:38,370
所以开起来的时候，你手里就一个方向盘，
So when you're going along, what you've got is a steering wheel

1061
00:50:38,594 --> 00:50:40,677
还有一个兼顾发动机熄火和开减速伞的手柄。
and a lever to stop the engine and pull the parachute.

1062
00:50:40,719 --> 00:50:41,752
其实挺简单的嘛。
So it's quite simple.

1063
00:50:41,786 --> 00:50:43,726
哈，比操控你屁股底下那把椅子还省事呢，伙计。
Oh, it's easier to control than your chair, mate.

1064
00:50:45,190 --> 00:50:47,484
行吧，那咱们就瞧瞧接下来发生了什么。
Ok, well, let's have a look what happened next.

1065
00:50:47,776 --> 00:50:50,155
我们把这个套上，呃……手穿过去就行。
Let us get these, err... just keep your arms through there.

1066
00:50:51,686 --> 00:50:52,499
这玩意儿干嘛用的？
What're they for?

1067
00:50:52,863 --> 00:50:53,735
这是手臂约束带，
These are arm strands

1068
00:50:54,395 --> 00:50:57,246
呃，万一车翻个底朝天的时候用。
Uh, in event if you're going upside down.

1069
00:50:58,134 --> 00:50:59,709
防止你的胳膊甩出驾驶舱。
They'll stop your arms coming out of the cockpit

1070
00:51:01,345 --> 00:51:02,572
我可不想翻个底朝天。
I don't want to go upside down.

1071
00:51:04,536 --> 00:51:05,171
油门
Throttle

1072
00:51:05,907 --> 00:51:07,355
设在半开。
Set to half.

1073
00:51:07,559 --> 00:51:09,176
好的，准备点火。
OK, so ignition

1074
00:51:12,214 --> 00:51:13,509
我的个老天爷啊。
Bloody hell fire.

1075
00:51:13,915 --> 00:51:15,168
这可是真真切切的喷气发动机。
That's a jet's engine.

1076
00:51:16,748 --> 00:51:18,187
我去。
Holy crap.

1077
00:51:20,199 --> 00:51:21,934
太吓人了！
This is terrifying!

1078
00:51:29,591 --> 00:51:31,094
要来了。动真格的了。
Here we go. This is it.

1079
00:51:33,541 --> 00:51:34,480
我的天呐。
Oh my god.

1080
00:51:35,411 --> 00:51:38,824
这感觉简直难以置信。整台车都在剧烈震颤。
The feel's just unbelievable. And it's vibrating.

1081
00:51:39,399 --> 00:51:42,184
我的天，我的老天哪！
Oh my God, Oh my God!

1082
00:51:44,250 --> 00:51:45,943
我能感觉到它在往右偏！
I can feel it pulling to the right!

1083
00:51:48,147 --> 00:51:49,592
我已经开上黑色沥青路面了。
I'm on the black tarmac.

1084
00:51:49,905 --> 00:51:54,485
要放减速伞了，我得开减速伞
/ / to use the parashute, I need a parachute

1085
00:51:59,562 --> 00:52:00,172
这……
That...

1086
00:52:01,323 --> 00:52:01,949
简直……
is...

1087
00:52:03,465 --> 00:52:04,413
噢，太不可思议了。
Oh, it's amazing.

1088
00:52:04,904 --> 00:52:07,020
啊……（深吸一口气）
Ah... (DEEP BREATH)

1089
00:52:10,881 --> 00:52:11,880
啊——！
Ahhh!

1090
00:52:11,888 --> 00:52:14,292
我只想再快一点。
I just want to go faster.

1091
00:52:15,085 --> 00:52:16,076
再快点。
More speed.

1092
00:52:16,220 --> 00:52:17,151
刚才有多快？
How quick was that.

1093
00:52:17,278 --> 00:52:19,028
呃，跑了220.4。
Eh, that's 220.4.

1094
00:52:22,939 --> 00:52:24,317
- 220？
- 没错。
- 220.
- Yeah.

1095
00:52:25,714 --> 00:52:26,867
如今在我们……
Now we are achieving...

1096
00:52:27,366 --> 00:52:30,160
自家的测试跑道上，也能跑到差不多接近这个速度了。
pretty close to that kind of speed now on our own runway here.

1097
00:52:30,331 --> 00:52:32,727
那你觉得在咱们这儿开兰博，跟开那玩意儿有什么区别？
So what's the difference you say a Lambo here and that?

1098
00:52:32,761 --> 00:52:35,285
区别就在于喷气发动机输出动力的方式。
It's just the way the jet engine delivers the power.

1099
00:52:35,285 --> 00:52:37,173
你能真切感受到那股力量是何等浩瀚。
You're aware that there is so much of it.

1100
00:52:37,190 --> 00:52:39,201
就是源源不断倾泻而出的庞大动力。
Just a huge amount of power going on.

1101
00:52:39,252 --> 00:52:41,572
所以更多的是那种震撼感，而非实际的速度数字。
So it's a sensation of that more than the actual speed.

1102
00:52:41,868 --> 00:52:44,946
不过你怎么知道什么时候该拉减速伞扳柄呢？
How did you know though when to pull the parachute lever.

1103
00:52:45,327 --> 00:52:47,668
呃，我们在跑道上摆了几个锥桶，所以……
En, well we just put some cones out on the runway so...

1104
00:52:47,703 --> 00:52:49,546
换作是我，肯定老早就拉了。
You see I would have pull it much sooner than that.

1105
00:52:49,690 --> 00:52:50,850
“我刚起步！伞就放出去了！”
I'm off! It's gone.

1106
00:52:52,356 --> 00:52:54,545
我甚至会在发车前就先拉开。以防万一嘛。
I'd pulled it before I set off. Just in case.

1107
00:52:55,722 --> 00:52:58,143
事后想想，呃，对……或许真是个更好的主意。
With hindsight, yeah. Bet... better idea perhaps.

1108
00:52:58,358 --> 00:53:01,626
好吧，所以下一次你就要开加力燃烧室了。
OK, so next time it was the afterburner.

1109
00:53:01,778 --> 00:53:02,714
对，没错。
Yes, absolutely.

1110
00:53:02,917 --> 00:53:04,559
短片里能看到那个画面，是吧？
And you can see that in the film, can you?

1111
00:53:04,585 --> 00:53:08,361
能，只要一点火你就能看出来，因为发动机尾部会喷出一道巨焰。
Yeah, you'll see you'll know when it's lit because this flame's coming out of the back of the engine.

1112
00:53:08,513 --> 00:53:10,435
好的。现在我得向大家科普一下，免得有人不知道：
OK. Now I have to explain to everybody in case you don't know

1113
00:53:10,443 --> 00:53:13,775
加力燃烧室通常只会配备在速度最顶级的军用战机上。
An afterburner is really only fits to the fastest military jets.

1114
00:53:14,157 --> 00:53:16,452
或者，严格来说，协和式客机上也有。
Or, and Concord, actually, for that matter.

1115
00:53:16,485 --> 00:53:19,846
但比如“鹞”式垂直起降战机，就没有配备。
A Harrier jump jet, for instance, doesn't have one.

1116
00:53:20,083 --> 00:53:22,027
行吧，因为对它来说没那个必要。
Ok, it's not deemed necessary for that.

1117
00:53:22,272 --> 00:53:25,176
但他却打算在一辆车里点燃这玩意儿。
But he was about to light one in a car.

1118
00:53:26,266 --> 00:53:26,596
是的。
Yeah.

1119
00:53:27,722 --> 00:53:28,840
谁让我想这么干呢，
Well I wanted to do this,

1120
00:53:29,085 --> 00:53:29,745
而我现在确实在干了。
And now I am.

1121
00:53:29,974 --> 00:53:32,531
我……呃，要是说我不
I've emm... I'd be lying if I said I wasn't

1122
00:53:33,750 --> 00:53:34,732
害怕，那绝对是假话。
quite scared.

1123
00:53:36,494 --> 00:53:36,943
不过……
However...

1124
00:53:39,040 --> 00:53:42,079
我觉得关键在于，一旦起步，就没退路了。
I think it's the fact that once you started, that's it.

1125
00:53:42,153 --> 00:53:44,414
油门可容不得你犹犹豫豫。只要它一动，你就得豁出去冲。
You don't mess about with the throttle. Once it go, you go.

1126
00:53:46,081 --> 00:53:49,099
这就是，懂吧……孤注一掷。
That's, you know... commitment.

1127
00:53:50,928 --> 00:53:52,443
来了来了，走起，来吧！
Here we go, here we go, here we go, come on.

1128
00:53:53,577 --> 00:53:54,993
就是现在，我得出发了。
This is it. I've got to be going.

1129
00:53:58,625 --> 00:54:00,084
噢！哈哈哈哈！
Ohh Hahaaaa!

1130
00:54:25,851 --> 00:54:31,190
你……
You /

1131
00:54:31,215 --> 00:54:33,899
天哪，我没法形容。我……
Yes, I can't describe. I...

1132
00:54:35,255 --> 00:54:36,720
我觉得我都要哭了。
I think I'm gonna cry.

1133
00:54:37,939 --> 00:54:39,065
我真没开玩笑。
I'm not joking.

1134
00:54:39,188 --> 00:54:42,345
我全身上下的每一个细胞……
Every part of my body is full...

1135
00:54:43,016 --> 00:54:43,930
都塞满了肾上腺素！
of adrenaline

1136
00:54:45,081 --> 00:54:46,283
噢，太爽了！
Oh, yes.

1137
00:54:46,749 --> 00:54:49,965
活着的感觉真好，太痛快了！
I'm so alive. I'm so alive.

1138
00:55:08,046 --> 00:55:09,926
刚才那一下看着可真够快的。
Now that looked really quick.

1139
00:55:10,019 --> 00:55:12,464
那趟更快，跑到了时速314英里。
That was quicker. That was 314 miles an hour.

1140
00:55:13,260 --> 00:55:18,077
这算得上是全英国有史以来速度最快的陆地行驶了吧？
And that is the fastest anyone's actually traveled in Britain before, isn't it?

1141
00:55:18,339 --> 00:55:19,707
呃，从技术层面上讲，我觉得算。
Well, technically, I suppose it is.

1142
00:55:19,707 --> 00:55:22,570
因为之前的英国陆地极速纪录是时速301英里。
'Cause I think the British land speed record is 301 miles an hour.

1143
00:55:22,570 --> 00:55:23,801
- 就那辆车跑出来的？
- 对。
- In that car?
- Yes.

1144
00:55:23,801 --> 00:55:25,911
- 没人能打破了。
- 没错，短期内恐怕没人了，没有。
- Nobody's gonna beat it.
- No, probably not now. No.

1145
00:55:27,511 --> 00:55:29,814
但要想成为官方纪录，你必须
But to be an official record, you've got do

1146
00:55:29,814 --> 00:55:32,996
反方向再跑一趟，然后取两次时速的平均值。
another run in the other direction then take an average of the 2 speeds.

1147
00:55:33,005 --> 00:55:35,858
但从遥测数据我们确切知道那是314，
The worse we know from telemetry that that was 314,

1148
00:55:35,884 --> 00:55:38,043
- 没错！
- 这就是全英国有人跑过的最快速度。
- Oh yeah!
- that's the fastest anyone's ever traveled.

1149
00:55:38,242 --> 00:55:39,960
对，但这终究……你知道的，不算官方纪录。
Oh yeah, but it's not, you know, official record.

1150
00:55:40,392 --> 00:55:41,332
那感觉究竟如何？
So what's it feel like?

1151
00:55:42,008 --> 00:55:43,142
呃，快呗。
Eh, fast.

1152
00:55:43,523 --> 00:55:47,173
呃，其实……我倒不是为了破纪录，
Eh, it's... I weren't trying to set a record.

1153
00:55:47,173 --> 00:55:49,018
我就是想体验一下极致的快。
I just wanted to get really really fast.

1154
00:55:49,077 --> 00:55:51,083
- 可你都跑到了314。
- 是啊。
- But you did 314
- Yeah.

1155
00:55:51,354 --> 00:55:53,868
- 而且你也见识到了极致速度是啥滋味。
- 没错。
- and you wanted to know what it was like to go really fast.
- Yeah.

1156
00:55:53,885 --> 00:55:54,994
那你愿望已经达成了。
So you'd found out.

1157
00:55:55,460 --> 00:55:57,875
你干嘛不直接钻进车里回家呢？
Why didn't you just get in your car and go home?

1158
00:55:58,688 --> 00:55:59,772
我其实也不知道。
I don't know really.

1159
00:56:00,009 --> 00:56:02,777
呃，问题是，你们刚刚看到的那趟
Emm, the thing is that run that you just saw

1160
00:56:02,811 --> 00:56:07,028
是在下午五点跑的，而跑道我们租到了五点半。
that was at 5 o'clock and we had the runway until 5:30.

1161
00:56:07,308 --> 00:56:07,753
然后……
And...

1162
00:56:09,886 --> 00:56:11,613
我现在当然想明白了，
I know now obviously,

1163
00:56:11,655 --> 00:56:14,044
呃，我说不好，我觉得这有点像……你知道的，小时候，
Eh, I don't know, I think it's a bit like, you know, when you were a kid,

1164
00:56:14,044 --> 00:56:15,288
你跟小伙伴们在外面野，
and you are out playing with your mates.

1165
00:56:15,407 --> 00:56:17,864
老妈扯着嗓子喊你回家吃晚饭。
And then your Mom would shout for you to come in for your tea.

1166
00:56:17,898 --> 00:56:20,548
你就非要再多逞能一会儿，赖着不走。
And you just pushing a bit and keep going a bit longer.

1167
00:56:20,677 --> 00:56:22,759
而摔下树往往就在这种时候。
And that's always when you fall out of the tree.

1168
00:56:23,521 --> 00:56:25,584
事后诸葛亮来看，确实是。
With hindsight again, yes

1169
00:56:25,906 --> 00:56:28,940
行吧，那接下来就是正戏了，是吧？
Well, alright. I suppose this it is then, isn't it really now?

1170
00:56:29,194 --> 00:56:30,490
接下来发生的就是这个，没错。
This is what happened next, yeah.

1171
00:56:57,880 --> 00:56:59,489
当时一切发生得太快，所以……
It was all over quite quickly so

1172
00:56:59,531 --> 00:57:00,818
咱们慢动作再放一遍。
do it again in slow motion.

1173
00:57:01,165 --> 00:57:04,396
你能看到爆胎的那一瞬间。
You can see the moment when the tire goes.

1174
00:57:04,396 --> 00:57:06,528
此时车速依然有288英里（约463公里）。
It's still doing 288 miles an hour here.

1175
00:57:07,247 --> 00:57:09,703
但接着就失控了，彻底甩了出去。
But then it's off. It's away.

1176
00:57:10,041 --> 00:57:13,754
我觉得从爆胎到彻底失控，实际上也就0.4秒左右。
I think it's about 0.4 of a second really from the tire blowing to it all going wrong.

1177
00:57:15,252 --> 00:57:18,265
接着车头啃进草地，整辆车开始翻滚。
Then when it digs in on the grass, the car rolls.

1178
00:57:18,612 --> 00:57:22,279
在草地上底朝天狂滑的时候，车速居然还有230英里，
It's still doing 230 when it's upside down on the grass

1179
00:57:23,795 --> 00:57:27,732
也就是说……看这里，车底朝天滑行时依然有230英里时速。
which is so... here now it's still doing 230 mph when it's upside and down.

1180
00:57:28,401 --> 00:57:29,643
接着又连翻了几下。
Then it flips a bit.

1181
00:57:30,870 --> 00:57:33,029
然后总算停下了。
And then it settles down.

1182
00:57:33,116 --> 00:57:36,849
防滚架连带着我的脑袋一起刨进地里，于是车停得相当快，
And the rollbar digs into the ground along with my head. And that stops it very quickly,

1183
00:57:38,493 --> 00:57:39,657
确实。
Indeed.

1184
00:57:41,760 --> 00:57:42,499
噢，谢谢大家。
Oh, thank you.

1185
00:57:54,659 --> 00:57:57,131
最惨的是，这本该是
The tragedy is, that would be

1186
00:57:57,606 --> 00:57:59,663
全英国有史以来速度最快的车祸。
the fastest car crash ever in Britain.

1187
00:58:00,036 --> 00:58:03,134
可吉尼斯世界纪录的人说，你必须往反方向再开一次才算数。
But Guinness Book of Records' people saying you got do it going in the other direction.

1188
00:58:05,407 --> 00:58:07,583
我才不稀罕这纪录！鬼才想要啊！
I don't want the record. It's not what I want.

1189
00:58:07,972 --> 00:58:10,199
所以你拼了老命折腾这一遭，
So you've come away with no record at all

1190
00:58:10,207 --> 00:58:12,952
连个纪录都没捞着，这可真够悲催的。
for having done that. That's a bit of a tragedy.

1191
00:58:13,468 --> 00:58:15,077
不过话说回来，我能问一句吗？
The thing is though, can I just ask,

1192
00:58:15,610 --> 00:58:18,446
咱们再看一遍出事的这一趟，
you can see again in the crash run,

1193
00:58:18,448 --> 00:58:19,523
好，就是你跑的最后一趟。
Ok, your last run.

1194
00:58:20,031 --> 00:58:22,918
这轮胎分明已经开始散架了。
The tire is starting to come apart.

1195
00:58:22,977 --> 00:58:25,618
好，仔细看就能发现，瞧，右边那条轮胎。
Ok, if we watch this you can see it, look at it, on the right end tyre.

1196
00:58:25,864 --> 00:58:26,651
看那儿。
Look there.

1197
00:58:27,792 --> 00:58:28,664
那么，
Now

1198
00:58:28,952 --> 00:58:29,560
抱歉啊哥们儿，
I'm sorry mate,

1199
00:58:30,000 --> 00:58:31,617
你当时怎么就瞎了没瞧见呢？
why didn't you spot that.

1200
00:58:31,812 --> 00:58:32,193
呃……
Well...

1201
00:58:33,014 --> 00:58:36,544
我当时什么都不知道，我正以288英里的时速狂飙呢。
I hadn't known all. I was doing 288 miles an hour.

1202
00:58:36,595 --> 00:58:37,364
得了吧。
I can have a lot.

1203
00:58:37,364 --> 00:58:39,904
我坐在办公室里，孩子们在叫嚷，我写着稿子，还打着电话，
I'm in the office the kids are shouting, I'm writting a story and I'm on the phone.

1204
00:58:39,921 --> 00:58:42,935
就算进来一头狮子，我都能注意得到。
If a lion walks in I'm going to notice it.

1205
00:58:43,349 --> 00:58:47,262
从爆胎开始到事故发生，中间只有0.4秒。
It was 0.4 of a second from the tire started to go to the accident started.

1206
00:58:47,516 --> 00:58:48,202
我本来能救回来的。
I could have held it.

1207
00:58:50,310 --> 00:58:52,317
怎么救，来一把全世界最长的动力漂移？
What, in the world's longest power slide?

1208
00:58:52,740 --> 00:58:55,449
顺便再跟我们念叨一下车价，顺带吐槽后备箱根本没空间？
Whilst telling us about the price and there was no room in the boot?

1209
00:58:55,483 --> 00:58:57,082
- 小菜一碟。
- 必须的。
- Easy-peasy.
- Yeah.

1210
00:58:57,083 --> 00:58:58,031
但问题是，
The problem is

1211
00:58:58,353 --> 00:59:01,714
归根结底是因为你当时没垫欧盟规定的儿童安全增高垫。
fundamentally you weren't wearing your EU booster seat.

1212
00:59:01,833 --> 00:59:04,230
你坐得太矮了，根本看不着路。
You were too low and you couldn't see it.

1213
00:59:04,264 --> 00:59:05,890
我要是真垫了增高垫，
If I had a booster seat on,

1214
00:59:05,932 --> 00:59:08,101
等车最后翻滚的时候，我脑袋早就搬家了。
my head would have come off when it rolled eventually.

1215
00:59:08,194 --> 00:59:09,472
你读过《公路交规》吗？
Have you read the highway codes?

1216
00:59:09,523 --> 00:59:11,258
呃，我当时身上又没带着。
Well, I didn't have a copy with me.

1217
00:59:11,284 --> 00:59:12,977
因为这上面写得清清楚楚：
Because it quite plainly says here,

1218
00:59:13,205 --> 00:59:16,647
“当车辆失控时，顺着打滑方向反打方向盘。”
When the car goes out of control, steer into the skid.

1219
00:59:17,747 --> 00:59:18,653
他说得对。
He's right.

1220
00:59:18,772 --> 00:59:20,963
听着，负责分析车上遥测数据的专家们——
Look, the expert guys that did the telemetry that was on the car

1221
00:59:20,980 --> 00:59:22,266
就是车载电脑那一帮人，
you know the computers and stuff,

1222
00:59:22,368 --> 00:59:25,155
他们说我的反应速度堪比战斗机飞行员。
they said I had the reactions of a fighter pilot.

1223
00:59:28,163 --> 00:59:30,508
他们可没说是一战时期的战斗机飞行员。
They didn't say it was a World War I fighter pilot.

1224
00:59:32,463 --> 00:59:37,360
开着索普威思“骆驼”、拉着木制操纵杆的那种，一点没错。
Riding-my-Sopwith-Camel-wooden-controls fighter pilot, exactly.

1225
00:59:37,487 --> 00:59:40,936
不，我觉得咱们完全可以坐在这儿，像过去几个月那样可劲儿挖苦你。
No, I think we could sit here as we have done for the last few months to take the Mickey out of you.

1226
00:59:40,936 --> 00:59:43,288
但事实是，我只想说：
The fact is though I would just like to say:

1227
00:59:43,929 --> 00:59:45,817
敢坐进那台鬼玩意儿里，你真挺有种的。
you were very brave to getting in that thing.

1228
